  (label "RS485_B" (at 171.45 80.01 0) (fields_autoplaced)
    (effects
      (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 2a736a02-d953-5ec4-897b-62f31f5caf77))
  (text "Smart port pins (VEX cables are straight-through)\n1 = RS-485 A (non-inverting)    2 = RS-485 B (inverting)\n3 = GND                         4 = raw battery, 10 to 14.6 V\nContact order A, B, GND, + as in the labelled VEX Forum cable photo\n(black A, red B, green GND, yellow +).\n\nU3 ~{RE} tied low, so the receiver is always on.\nR3 holds DE low: the board boots listen-only.\nR4 is DNP. Fit it only for cables over 750 mm.\nU3 MAX33071E: A/B survive +/-65 V even unpowered, so a miswired\ncable cannot kill it. Cheaper drop-in: ST3485EBDR (14 V max)." (at 55.88 78.74 0)
    (effects
      (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid fb7e68c7-10c6-5b95-b6e5-ab668ae4eb8c))
